WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:05.265
During the time that Edward was away from the palace, what had happened to Tom?

2
00:00:05.266 --> 00:00:09.110
Did he ever think about Edward, the real king?

3
00:00:09.111 --> 00:00:15.567
At first Tom did think about the young prince who had treated him so kindly.

4
00:00:15.568 --> 00:00:21.915
But every day brought Tom a new and more exciting experience.

5
00:00:21.916 --> 00:00:27.596
His confidence increased until he no longer feared being discovered as an imposter.

6
00:00:27.597 --> 00:00:31.980
So Edward gradually faded from Tom's mind.

7
00:00:31.981 --> 00:00:40.557
When the day of the coronation arrived, Tom was happy in his role and looking forward to being crowned.

8
00:00:40.558 --> 00:00:45.777
The day began with a grand parade through the city.

9
00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:51.494
Wearing a splendid outfit, Tom waved to the crowd from a white horse.

10
00:00:51.495 --> 00:00:55.378
"This is all for me!" he thought proudly.

11
00:00:55.379 --> 00:00:59.605
"A few weeks ago, I would have hated all the attention.

12
00:00:59.606 --> 00:01:06.886
Today I didn't even mind that it took lots of servants three hours to dress me!"

13
00:01:06.887 --> 00:01:12.718
As Tom scanned the crowd, he suddenly spotted his best friend from Offal Street.

14
00:01:12.719 --> 00:01:19.831
"Oh, I wish I could wave and Julian would recognize me!" Tom thought wistfully.

15
00:01:19.832 --> 00:01:27.662
"Julian would be so surprised to learn that his old friend is about to be crowned king—for real!"

16
00:01:27.663 --> 00:01:33.792
However, Tom also knew that if Julian did recognize him, his reign might be over.

17
00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:38.920
"Good-bye, Julian," Tom said quietly without waving.

18
00:01:38.921 --> 00:01:43.519
Lord Hertford rode up beside Tom, interrupting his thoughts.

19
00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:48.765
"This is quite a day, Your Majesty," Lord Hertford said.

20
00:01:48.766 --> 00:01:55.915
"The weather is perfect, and your people are delighted to see you smiling and looking so well."

21
00:01:55.916 --> 00:02:00.392
Lord Hertford handed Tom a small leather pouch.

22
00:02:00.393 --> 00:02:04.593
"Here's some money for you to toss to the people."

23
00:02:04.594 --> 00:02:09.692
Tom reached into the pouch and threw some coins to the crowd.

24
00:02:09.693 --> 00:02:17.086
A loud cheer went up, and Tom happily waved.

25
00:02:17.087 --> 00:02:22.996
He was just about to toss more coins, when he noticed a familiar woman staring at him.

26
00:02:22.997 --> 00:02:25.415
"Mother!" Tom thought.

27
00:02:25.416 --> 00:02:30.499
His hand flew up to his face, covering his eyes with the palm out.

28
00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:36.880
Recognizing the gesture that Tom had always made when startled, his mother ran toward him.

29
00:02:36.881 --> 00:02:41.116
"Oh, Tom, my dear son!" she cried.

30
00:02:41.117 --> 00:02:45.116
"I knew I'd find you if I kept looking!"

31
00:02:45.117 --> 00:02:52.695
Tom barely glanced at her as he rode on. "I don't know you, woman!"

32
00:02:52.696 --> 00:02:56.687
A guard grabbed Tom's mother and pushed her back into the crowd.

33
00:02:56.688 --> 00:02:59.805
"Get away from the king!"

34
00:02:59.806 --> 00:03:05.211
Tom's heart broke to see his mother treated like that, but what could he do?

35
00:03:05.212 --> 00:03:08.947
He turned in the saddle for one last glimpse of her.

36
00:03:08.948 --> 00:03:14.411
She seemed brokenhearted, and he was filled with shame.

37
00:03:14.412 --> 00:03:20.946
After exchanging clothes with Edward, Tom had thought about his mother and sister, Nancy, every day.

38
00:03:20.947 --> 00:03:26.665
But eventually he had forgotten about them, just as he had forgotten Edward.

39
00:03:26.666 --> 00:03:33.374
"What's the point of being king if I must pretend that I don't know my own mother?" Tom thought.

40
00:03:33.375 --> 00:03:40.249
"I wish I'd never gone inside the palace. I don't want to be king anymore!"

41
00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:44.653
The parade wound its way through the streets toward the cathedral.

42
00:03:44.654 --> 00:03:49.268
People cheered and applauded, but the king rode with his head bowed.

43
00:03:49.269 --> 00:03:53.830
He kept seeing his mother's face and how wounded she'd looked.

44
00:03:53.831 --> 00:03:58.408
"Money! Give us money!" someone called out.

45
00:03:58.409 --> 00:04:03.988
"Long live King Edward!" someone else cried.

46
00:04:03.989 --> 00:04:08.132
But those voices were drowned out by the ones in Tom's head.

47
00:04:08.133 --> 00:04:15.541
He kept hearing his mother calling his name, and then his own voice saying, "I don't know you, woman!"

48
00:04:15.542 --> 00:04:23.058
As Tom rode along, unsmiling and slumped in the saddle, people began to notice that something was wrong.

49
00:04:23.059 --> 00:04:27.847
"The king doesn't look so good," one woman said to another.

50
00:04:27.848 --> 00:04:34.867
"Maybe the rumors about his health are true," the second woman said.

51
00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:40.997
"Your Majesty, this is not the time for daydreaming," Lord Hertford said.

52
00:04:40.998 --> 00:04:47.015
"People see your unhappy face and take it as a bad omen for your reign.

53
00:04:47.016 --> 00:04:52.798
You must sit up straight and smile! Toss them some more coins."

54
00:04:52.799 --> 00:04:57.014
Tom did as he was told, tossing coins and smiling.

55
00:04:57.015 --> 00:05:02.313
But there was no longer any joy in his smile or his heart.

56
00:05:02.314 --> 00:05:08.236
Just before they reached the cathedral, Lord Hertford had to remind him of his duty.

57
00:05:08.237 --> 00:05:11.760
"Come on, sir!" Lord Hertford urged Tom.

58
00:05:11.761 --> 00:05:15.302
"You've let some dreadful pauper upset you.

59
00:05:15.303 --> 00:05:22.110
Forget about her and think about this: you're about to be crowned king!"

60
00:05:22.111 --> 00:05:27.009
"She isn't just some pauper," Tom said in a flat voice.

61
00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.653
"She's my mother!"

62
00:05:29.654 --> 00:05:36.576
"Oh no!" Lord Hertford was so shocked that he pulled his horse to the side of the road.

63
00:05:36.577 --> 00:05:41.136
"I'd hoped that the king was cured," he thought.

64
00:05:41.137 --> 00:05:45.507
"But instead his illness has obviously returned.

65
00:05:45.508 --> 00:05:50.334
What a terrible day for this to happen!"

